  "body": "### Summary\nAs a Favoris reader who sorts by last post, I want legacy's toolbar button that shows my favourites grouped by category for the moment, without changing my sort setting, so that I can glance at one category and go back to my usual list.\n\nRefs #655 (inventory row 44).\n\n### Legacy (reference `87fe0d1c`)\n- Added by `d645f525` (before it, the button was disabled in the flat sort). `HFRswift/Swift/Favorites.swift` @ `87fe0d1c`:\n  - `:462` `@State private var showsCategoriesOnDemand = false` (memory only, not a setting);\n  - `:488-494` `usesCategorizedFavoritesList = favoritesSortedByCategories || showsCategoriesOnDemand`; the same button means « sections repliées » in the grouped sort;\n  - `:796-798` the on-demand view resets when the sort setting changes;\n  - `:808-846` the toolbar button: grouped sort → toggles « Afficher / Masquer les sections repliées »; flat sort → toggles the on-demand categories, labels « Afficher toutes les catégories » / « Masquer les catégories » (symbol `list.bullet.circle` / `.fill`).\n\n### SwiftHFR today (`dev-swift` @ `e672de7c`)\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Root/RootTabsView.swift:149-150`: the Favoris « Options » menu has the persistent toggles « Trier par catégorie » (`sujets_avec_cat`) and « Afficher les sections repliées ». Nothing shows the categories temporarily; LOT-124 (`docs/lots/LOT-124-favourites-options.md`, Behaviour) does not mention legacy's temporary view, and no GAP row does.\n\n### Decision needed (operator)\n1. Port legacy's temporary view (a button or a menu item, memory only, reset when the sort changes), or\n2. Keep the persistent « Trier par catégorie » toggle as the way to see categories, and record it as a documented difference (GAP row, `b`).\n\n### Acceptance criteria (option 1)\n- With « Trier par catégorie » off, one control shows the list grouped by category with legacy's labels; tapping it again, changing the sort or relaunching goes back to the flat list; the setting is never written.\n- A pure test pins the rule (`FavoritesPresentation`); `// Port of HFRswift/Swift/Favorites.swift (… :808-846) @ 87fe0d1c` header.\n\n### Ledger (for the PR that closes this, either option)\n`gap-new` in the \"Lists\" section, id GAP-<this issue>.",
